USB MIDI host, the platform's side: an app switches the USB-C port between a device (the computer's) and the host
of a USB-MIDI device (plat.h plat_usb_host, plat_usb_host_state, plat_usb_host_event), with FM1B_USB_HOST 1 in its
app.h (default 0: nothing of it is built). Follows felucca-bsp's docs/USB_HOST.md: the main loop runs
usb_host_task before usb_retry, plat_midi_in consumes midi_usb_lost; TO_USB reaches the device through felucca-bsp's
midi_out_event. The host simulator has the same API and a "usbhost plug | nomidi | unplug" command.
The driver is felucca-bsp pull request #7 (patches/felucca-bsp/0001-usb-midi-host-pr7.patch, where its licence
is quoted); this patch is ignis32's (MPL-2.0) and holds none of its code.
Why MIDIMON needs it: a USB-MIDI controller or synth plugged into the FM-1 itself, monitored and reached by THRU.
Applies to: fm1-base aa2b3bc, with felucca-bsp d6b8f77 + its pull request #7. Upstream: not offered yet (keremimo
means to bring USB host to fm1-base).
